---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

/**
 * 410 GONE — deliberately, and deliberately not a redirect.
 *
 * This URL was in a sitemap that has already been submitted, so it cannot simply vanish:
 * a soft 404 (200 with an apology) leaves the URL indexed and competing, and a redirect to
 * an unrelated page is a lie about equivalence that Google eventually treats as a soft 404
 * anyway. 410 is the one signal that means "this existed, it is gone, stop asking" — it is
 * processed faster than 404 and it removes the URL rather than retrying it for weeks.
 *
 * Why it went: a liquidation-price calculator is a commodity. Every exchange ships one, they
 * all rank, and ours differed only in being arithmetically correct — which is not a reason
 * for a page to exist when the same correction is already stated, with live numbers, inside
 * every contract page's margin-tier section.
 *
 * The tier-correct margin maths itself stays in src/lib/margin.ts. It is what /funding/*,
 * /liquidations, /liquidations/survival and the surviving calculators are all built on; only
 * the public page is withdrawn.
 */
Astro.response.status = 410;
Astro.response.headers.set("cache-control", "public, max-age=3600");
---

<Base
  title="Removed"
  description="The liquidation price calculator has been withdrawn. The tier-correct liquidation price is shown on each perpetual's funding page instead."
  noindex
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/tools">Tools</a> › Liquidation price</p>
    <h1>This calculator has been removed</h1>
    <p>
      A standalone liquidation-price calculator is a commodity — every exchange ships one. The
      only thing ours did differently was use the published maintenance-margin tiers instead of
      the <code>entry × (1 ∓ 1/leverage)</code> formula, and that correction is more useful
      attached to a real contract than sitting on an empty form.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="banner">
    <div>
      <div class="banner__title">The same number, on a contract</div>
      <div class="banner__sub">
        Every contract page prints its tier-correct liquidation price and how far the common
        formula is wrong, against that contract's live mark and its own published tiers.
      </div>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/funding/btc">BTC margin tiers</a>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section">Still here</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" href="/tools/position-size">
      <div class="card__label">Position size</div>
      <div class="card__value" style="font-size:19px">Risk-based sizing</div>
      <div class="card__meta">Checks the stop against the tier-correct liquidation price.</div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/tools/leverage">
      <div class="card__label">Leverage</div>
      <div class="card__value" style="font-size:19px">What the tier allows</div>
      <div class="card__meta">The advertised maximum applies to the smallest tier only.</div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="/liquidations">
      <div class="card__label">Liquidation map</div>
      <div class="card__value" style="font-size:19px">Modelled density</div>
      <div class="card__meta">Where levels stand, and where price has already cleared them.</div>
    </a>
  </div>
</Base>
